@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Laya purpose suggestion service
+
+This is the deployable service for Route Finder, not an automatic immigration decision. Every suggestion requires a user click before it fills the existing purpose field. All existing route rules and manual choices remain available. No confidence threshold authorizes a choice: high-confidence mistakes were observed in the initial ten-case MCP test (5/10 correct). The renamed-label schema in this service has not been established as more accurate.
+
+## Contract and local use
+
+Python 3.13, `laya==0.3.5`, `uvicorn==0.53.0`. Install from `requirements.txt` in an isolated environment. A cached multilingual checkpoint is required; startup deliberately fails if it is absent. Runtime downloads and Hugging Face telemetry are disabled. Model import/load happens once during ASGI startup. Run **one worker**; additional workers duplicate model memory.
+
+```bash
+cd services/laya-purpose
+LAYA_DEVICE=cpu /path/to/venv/bin/uvicorn app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8011 --workers 1 --no-access-log --no-proxy-headers --limit-concurrency 16
+```
+
+`GET /healthz` returns readiness. `POST /api/purpose-suggestion/` accepts only JSON `{"text":"我想去德国读硕士。"}` with 1–300 trimmed Unicode characters and at most 4096 body bytes. It returns either `{"status":"suggestion","purpose":"university","requiresConfirmation":true}` or `{"status":"needs_clarification","purpose":null,"requiresConfirmation":true}`. Purpose IDs match the existing six select values. Extra fields, query strings, malformed JSON and unknown model labels fail closed. No generic prediction endpoint is exposed; users cannot supply model instructions.
+
+One inference runs at a time; simultaneous requests get 503 with no queue. The client aborts after 12 seconds and preserves manual use. A disconnected client does not kill the CPU operation: capacity stays occupied until inference completes. Monitor service health and resource use; terminate/restart a stuck process operationally. Health reports loaded state, not model accuracy or inference liveness. There is no database, text cache or application request logging. Do not enable request-body capture, debug logging, tracing, or access logs containing input at any proxy/APM layer.
+
+## Container deployment
+
+Build from this directory (`docker build -t visalang-laya-purpose .`). On the target architecture, provision the reviewed checkpoint into a Hugging Face cache directory before starting; make it readable to UID 10001. The cache is an operator-managed, read-only artifact. Record its exact revision/hash with the image digest in the release record; do not silently upgrade model weights. Configure `LAYA_MODEL` and `LAYA_SUBFOLDER` when using a different pinned local checkpoint. Memory/CPU limits below are starting allocations, not measured production sizing; validate on the target host.
+
+```bash
+docker run -d --name visalang-laya-purpose --restart unless-stopped \
+  --read-only --tmpfs /tmp:rw,noexec,nosuid,size=256m \
+  --cap-drop ALL --security-opt no-new-privileges \
+  --memory 4g --cpus 2 --pids-limit 128 \
+  -p 127.0.0.1:8011:8011 \
+  -v /srv/visalang/laya-cache:/models:ro \
+  visalang-laya-purpose
+```
+
+The image installs pinned top-level packages; transitive dependencies must be frozen by recording the built image digest for rollout and rollback. This task does not claim a Docker build or target-host capacity test unless recorded in the acceptance evidence.
+
+The repository uses Nginx. In its `http` context, add `limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=visalang_purpose:10m rate=6r/m;`. Install `deploy/laya-purpose-nginx.conf` and include it inside the canonical HTTPS server block. Existing `/api/purpose-suggestion/` requests must go to this service while all other routes stay static. Validate with `nginx -t` before an authorized reload. Behind a trusted CDN, configure real client IP handling explicitly or rate limiting may group visitors under a proxy address.
+
+For a separate machine, use a private network or authenticated TLS reverse proxy and restrict upstream access to the website proxy. Do not expose port 8011 publicly, enable wildcard CORS, or put service secrets in frontend code. The browser always uses the same-origin path; it never calls the operator's Codex MCP or workstation.
+
+Production activation requires explicit owner authorization plus model/cache readiness, real HTTP and browser tests, rate-limit checks, memory/load measurements, logging review, and a recorded previous release/image digest. Roll back by removing the API include and restoring the previous site release; manual selection continues working when the API is unavailable. A service suggestion is not a country, eligibility, exemption or certificate-acceptance decision.
+
+## Verification
+
+```bash
+python3 -m unittest discover -s services/laya-purpose -p 'test_*.py' -v
+node tests/laya-purpose.test.mjs
+```
+
+Run these commands from the repository root. The Python tests inject a predictor to exercise the HTTP boundary without downloading weights. Real-model smoke evidence and browser tests are recorded separately. No claim of improved intent accuracy follows from passing these contract tests.
